# Infrastructure Standards

## Docker

- Use multi-stage builds.
- Use minimal runtime images.
- Run services as non-root users.
- Pin important image versions.
- Use health checks.
- Avoid unnecessary exposed ports.

## Docker Compose

- Separate application and infrastructure services.
- Use persistent volumes.
- Use private internal networks.
- Keep secrets out of committed files.
- Define resource limits where supported.
- Use service health checks and appropriate dependencies.

## Nginx

- Use reverse proxy configuration.
- Apply request size limits.
- Configure sensible timeouts.
- Do not expose internal services directly.

## Deployment

- Local development uses Docker Compose.
- Production deployment will use a VPS.
- Production configuration must be separate.
- Never commit production credentials.